   distributed for any purpose and without charge, with or without
   modification, provided the copyright notices are retained; they are,
   above and in that file. No font is included: a PDF that names one of
   the fourteen standard fonts is drawn with the reader's own copy.

2. The shipping: launchers, installers and scripts

   rel/, .github/workflows/ and lib/polis/{updates,data_home,autostart,
   launcher_details}* came from Alnasl (https://github.com/teapot-chess/Alnasl),
   by the same owner; the join and the link
   (lib/polis/join.ex, lib/polis/link.ex) came from Arkab
   (https://github.com/teapot-chess/Arkab), likewise. Changes: the names,
   and what the program does.

3. What the Windows downloads carry besides Polis

   None of this is in the repository; the release workflow puts it in the
   installer and the zip.

   - Erlang/OTP's runtime (Apache-2.0) and the compiled dependencies listed
     in mix.lock, each under its own licence.
   - Velopack (https://github.com/velopack/velopack), MIT licence,
     Copyright (c) Velopack Ltd. and contributors: the installer and
     updater (Setup.exe, Update.exe, the stub beside them) and
     velopack_libc.dll, which the launcher loads to apply an update.
     rel/windows/launcher.c declares the part of its C interface it calls.
   - Microsoft's Visual C++ runtime (vcruntime140.dll, vcruntime140_1.dll,
     msvcp140.dll), which Erlang's Windows build needs, redistributed
     unchanged beside it as Microsoft's terms for those files allow.

On Windows, Polis prints through Windows' own printing (System.Drawing, run
by the Windows PowerShell every Windows 10 and 11 has) and the printer's own
driver; on macOS and Linux through CUPS. Neither is included.
